source: crates/rdlt-certify/tests/it/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&help.stdout)"
---
Certifies a connector against the protocol's conformance clauses

Usage: rdlt-certify [OPTIONS] [TARGET]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]  The connector: its binary's path, or the `grpcs://host:port` endpoint it listens at

Options:
      --role <ROLE>                Certify this role alone; by default, every role the connector serves [possible values: source, destination]
      --config <CONFIG>            The connector's configuration, as JSON [default: {}]
      --config-file <CONFIG_FILE>  A file holding the connector's configuration, as JSON
      --env <NAME>                 An environment variable a spawned connector keeps; it otherwise starts with none
      --tls-cert <TLS_CERT>        The host's certificate chain, in PEM, for an endpoint
      --tls-key <TLS_KEY>          The host's private key, in PEM, for an endpoint
      --tls-ca <TLS_CA>            The CA bundle that issued the connector's certificate, in PEM, for an endpoint
      --kill-seed <SEED>           Kills the connector at the points this seed draws, as a failed kill clause reports, to reproduce the failure
      --kill-timeout <SECONDS>     Gives each kill clause this many seconds for all its loads, rather than 300: a connector slower than about two seconds a commit needs more
      --require <REQUIRE>          What exits 0: `complete`, every clause that applies seen to be met; `partial`, none failed and one passed, whatever was not observed [default: complete] [possible values: complete, partial]
      --output <OUTPUT>            How to print the reports [default: plain] [possible values: plain, json]
      --clauses                    Prints every clause, in Markdown, and exits
  -h, --help                       Print help
  -V, --version                    Print version
